# x-rs-desktop-pet core wire

file: native/core/crates/mixdog-core-domains/src/domains/mod.rs
place: the `pub mod` list, after `pub mod client;`
add: pub mod desktop_pet;

file: native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs
place: fn real_core, after the registration of the other core-domains services (data dir `D` as for MigrateProfileService)
add: builder.register(Arc::new(mixdog_core_domains::domains::desktop_pet::DesktopPetService::new(data_dir.clone(), profile, changed, &tokens)))?;
note: `profile` is an Arc<dyn Fn() -> Option<PathBuf> + Send + Sync> answering the Electron profile directory the core has recorded or been named (the one MigrateProfileService reads: `<D>/migration/profile-gen.json` `profile`, else the late manifest's, else the manifest's `roots.profile`). The first `desktopPet/state/read` that finds no `<D>/desktop/desktop-pet.json` copies `<profile>/desktop-pet.json` there (create-only, the old file kept: the migration kind of this task; mixdog-migrate's supplement pass is untouched and still never opens desktop-pet.json). `changed` is an Arc<dyn Fn(&DesktopPetPrefs) + Send + Sync> publishing the server notification `desktopPet/state/changed` { prefs } on the app feed, the way `ui/settings/changed` is published.
remove from SERVICE_PENDING: "desktopPet/state/read", "desktopPet/state/write" (if listed)

file: native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol (pending-rows/x-rs-desktop-pet.rows)
note: the rows file carries the new src/v2/desktop_pet.rs (the types the service imports); PROTO-WIRE-G3 must apply it before the core compiles. No Cargo change: mixdog-core-domains already depends on mixdog-app-protocol, mixdog-statefile, mixdog-rt and mixdog-core-base.
